 deserve what he did to  them  after the opening we see willie tiber  preparing for his stage production  where he will be declaring war on  paradise island in front of journalists  and diplomats from all around the world  unlike his usual confident self willie  is visibly shaken in this moment  and it's not because he's afraid of  public speaking in episode 4 of the  final season  commander mcgath informed willy that  there was an infestation of rats in mali  by which he meant that there were spies  from paradise island currently in the  country  following on from that there was an  important conversation in the manga that  was presumably taken out of this episode  for pacing reasons  but mcgath says it's highly likely that  spies from parodies will attack  during the big speech mcgath believed  that willy would die  because they don't know exactly how  their enemy will attack and therefore  it's hard to protect him when he's just  you know front and center on stage  despite that willie accepted his fate  and considers his death to be necessary  to show the world  the genuine threat of paradise island  his death will make the world feel  sympathy for both willie himself  and the innocent eldians in liberio who  would be killed  that's why in this moment willie is so  nervous because he knows he's not making  it out of this performance alive  he's then approached by miss kiyomi who  was the lady in the last episode that  saved udo from getting punished  she's an ambassador from the nation of  hizuru which is the only place that is  tolerant of eldians and she tells willy  that she hopes the production goes well  after this she leaves the area without  sticking around for the performance  which is probably for the best moving on  rainer comes face to face with erin in  this dimly lit cellar  and he can barely believe what he's  seeing aaron orders rhinos to sit down  as if he was taking her hostage  and you can see that falco is confused  by their reactions as i explained in my  last review  falco believes that these two guys are  old friends so reina's blank expression  is not exactly what he was expecting  aaron explains that the cellar they're  in  is underneath a regular apartment  building behind the stage which is  basically a thinly veiled way of saying  he's about to kill everyone i love  falco's innocence in this moment  like he truly has no idea what's going  on as if this man is not about to go  full titan mode in a few minutes  obviously reiner is aware of the  situation so he complies with aaron's  request to sit down  followed by an awkward silence in which  falco offers to leave  however eren tells falco to stay and  listen to his story which was a mean  thing to do considering that aaron knows  he's about to blow this place up  did those letters mean nothing to you  the crowd continues to get seated for  the performance  and we get a brief interaction between  rhino's mother and annie's father  in season 1 we saw in a flashback how  annie's father made her promise to  return home from the mission  which is why she was crying as she was  about to be captured her father believes  that she must still be alive  because of the promise she made to  return home although reina's mother is  understandably not so sure  the leaders of mali's military were also  sitting by this point  and it was willie tiber's request that  all the leaders were grouped together as  close as possible  because willy knows the enemy is going  to attack he put the leaders in this  section as bait  so that they could be wiped out by the  enemy and then mcgath could rebuild the  military from scratch  just before the curtain rises an alden  soldier approaches the warriors of mali  and asks them to leave because commander  mcgath has summoned them we then go back  to eren falco and reiner  as the vice captain of the warriors  finally musters up the courage  to ask aaron what he came here to do  aaron replies in epic fashion  by telling reina that 