are  that the warriors have disappeared this  is a clear sign that the enemies are  about to attack  with poco and peak still being stuck  underground the reason they're not able  to turn into titans is due to the  cramped conditions  and even if they could transform they  just end up crushing each other in the  process so  it wouldn't be worth it in the cellar  aaron whips out his amputated leg  and begins regeneration over the last  couple weeks i had a bunch of people  asking me why aaron's leg hasn't healed  yet and the answer is that he was  choosing not to do so because as we saw  in the past  titan shifters can delay their healing  process if they want to  by this point falco totally realizes  he's been tricked and you got to feel  bad for him because  he was genuinely encouraged by mr  kruger's words and he thought the two  had formed a real friendship  erin reveals that the letters falco sent  for him were not for his family like he  claimed but instead they were for his  friends  reiner briefly ponders what that could  mean before the scene switches over to  willie tiber who explains to the world  that aaron has the potential to activate  the rumbling willy's logic  is that to eliminate the threat from  parody's island they need to stop aaron  before he has a chance to activate the  titans in the walls  aaron even admits to falco and reiner  that it is a possibility that he could  do this  he says that while he's the bad guy now  reina annie and belto were the bad guys  to him  when they breached the walls all those  years ago and caused his mother to be  eaten  when questioned reiner claims they only  breached the walls to rotate the  founding titan  and save the world in the process you  can see that eren almost takes pity on  reiner as he did earlier in the episode  and he says that reiner must not have  had a choice both of these men used to  believe  that the people across the ocean were  the enemy but after spending a lot of  time in mali  aaron came to realize that all aldians  are the same there are both good  and bad people on both sides of the  ocean and to eren  reiner was just an ignorant kid who  didn't know what he was doing when he  breached the walls  this is the moment when rhino really  loses it and reveals the truth to aaron  after all these years  which is that the mission was going to  be abandoned after marcel's death  and the only reason why everything  happened was because reiner convinced  them to continue  part of that reason was that rhino  wanted to survive but as he admits here  he also wanted to be a hero that people  respected it wasn't his age or his  environment that made him make that  decision  so reiner actually takes responsibility  and asks erin to kill him  definitely not how falco thought this  reunion would go but life comes at you  fast  meanwhile willie tiber gets the crowd on  his side by admitting that the danger  facing the world is due to the alien  race  and that if it was up to him he would  have chosen never to have been born  that said because he was born willie now  doesn't want to die  understandably and he encourages all  other nations that want to live  to join hands with mali and ensure a  future together  honestly this was a great speech because  he knows that people hate aldians  so he's admitting their faults but at  the same time unifying everyone against  a common enemy  in the cellar aaron asks a suicidal  rhino to stand up  and says that he finally understands him  like reiner  aaron is also a person who keeps moving  forward until his enemies are destroyed  and without hesitation he activates his  titan transformation  just as willie declares war on parody's  island i absolutely love the slow motion  in this moment  and it was also a bit unlucky for those  soldiers who were standing right outside  the door  the attack titan manifest itself  completely destroying the cellar that  reiner and falco were in  as well as the building full of  civilians aaron emerges in front of  diplomats and journalists from all  around the world before crushing the  stage and willie tiber  with his bare hands this moment is so  iconic  so it was great to see it finally  animated and yeah in my opinion i think  it was done  incredibly well let me know what you  guys think in the comments down below  and as usual i'd appreciate if you  dropped a like if you like this video  and share it with anyone who you think  might enjoy it thanks for watching and  until the next one  peace out

